<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<menu xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto">

    <item
        android:id="@+id/menu_voice_search"
        android:icon="@drawable/ic_mic"
        android:iconTint="@android:color/white"
        android:title="@string/voice_search"
        app:showAsAction="always" />

    <!-- ⚠⚠ THE AFFORDANCE MOVED HERE FROM THE ROWS, AND IT MOVED BECAUSE THE ROW VERSION LIED.
         item_quick_search_query.xml and item_quick_search_media.xml each carried a per-row close (✕)
         button wired to QuickSearchClient.deleteQuickSearch. Deezer's implementation IGNORES the item it is
         handed and calls user.clearSearchHistory — an ACCOUNT-WIDE wipe — so an ✕ on one chip, and an ✕ on
         a suggested TRACK row, both destroyed every entry the user had. The icon promised per-item removal
         on two surfaces and delivered a bulk destructive action on both.
         A confirmation dialog was considered and rejected: an ✕ whose dialog says "this clears everything"
         is an affordance that contradicts itself, and users trust the icon over the dialog.
         ⚠️ ANYONE RESTORING A PER-ROW ✕ IS RESTORING THAT BUG unless a per-entry deletion method exists by
         then — see the note at DeezerExtension.deleteQuickSearch for why none is known.
         KNOWN LOSS, NAMED RATHER THAN GLOSSED: extensions WITHOUT QuickSearchClient (Offline, Unified) fall
         through to SearchViewModel.defaultDeleteSearch, which removes ONE entry from a local list
         correctly. Removing the ✕ takes that working capability away from them to stop Deezer's broken one.
         Accepted deliberately: one honest bulk action beats a per-item action that works on two extensions
         and lies on the one people actually use.

         ⚠⚠ OPEN TV ITEM — NOT CHECKED, AND THE DIRECTION IS UNFAVOURABLE. NOTHING BELOW IS VERIFIED; it is
         written as the honest state so a future TV pass picks it up rather than re-deriving it.
           • THE OLD ✕ WAS PROBABLY REACHABLE. It sat inside each row of the overlay RecyclerView, which
             already has D-pad wiring (QuickSearchAdapter's O6 onFirstRowUp), so a D-pad user in the list
             could plausibly reach it with RIGHT from a focused row.
           • THIS MENU ITEM PROBABLY IS NOT. It lives in the SearchView's TOOLBAR — a different surface, with
             no app-directed focus entry except onFirstRowUp landing on the EDIT TEXT. Getting from there to
             here needs three unverified links: geometric RIGHT from the edit text into the ActionMenuView,
             the overflow button being focusable, and the popup being D-pad navigable. `never` puts this in
             the overflow, so it is strictly deeper than the mic item beside it (`always`, a visible button)
             — and the mic is NOT evidence either, since a TV often has no microphone and that item may never
             have been exercised on one.
           • SO THIS CHANGE MAY REMOVE THE ONLY TV-REACHABLE ROUTE TO CLEARING SEARCH HISTORY, rather than
             being neutral. Consequence if true: a TV user cannot clear their search history at all.
           • KNOWINGLY NOT SPENT ON (2026-09-10): effectively no TV users, and that consequence does not
             justify a build. Recorded, not fixed.
           HOW A TV PASS WOULD CHECK IT, cheapest first: focus the search field, DOWN into the list, UP back
           (confirms the O6 baseline), then RIGHT from the edit text — if focus reaches the mic, link one
           holds and the rest is likely; if it does not, the toolbar menu is unreachable on TV TODAY,
           independently of this change, and the action needs to live in the suggestions LIST instead, which
           is provably reachable. Making this item icon + `ifRoom` rather than `never` would collapse three
           unverified links to one at the cost of a second visible button on phone. -->
    <item
        android:id="@+id/menu_clear_search_history"
        android:title="@string/clear_search_history"
        app:showAsAction="never" />

</menu>
